    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n56757" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κερᾱτ-ίνης</span></b>  [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῐ], <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ου</span>, ὁ</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>the fallacy called the
				Horns</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἴ τι οὐκ ἀπέβαλες, τοῦτο ἔχεις:
					κέρατα δὲ οὐκ ἀπέβαλες: κέρατα ἄρα ἔχεις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.L.
					7.187
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κερατίνας ἐρωτῶν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Com.Adesp.</u>
					294
				</span></i>
			: acc.sg. -<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ναν</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Symp.</u>
				23
			</span></i>; cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κερατίς</span>.</div>
